#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:406
msgid "Hooks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:407
msgid "Core exposes runtime hooks and configuration filters for addons. Below is the consolidated list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:410
msgid "(filter) Allow addons to provide a deterministic question set for a level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:414
msgid "(filter) Allow addons to register their own shortcode-based Gutenberg blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:418
msgid "(action) Fired when the final set is fixed; consume context for logging."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:422
msgid "(filter) The questions about to be sent to the browser, after the questions cache. Use it to localize or adjust the content. Never change the ids, their order, the number of options or the \"answer\" index: scoring is done server-side from the ids and the option indexes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:426
msgid "(action) A question was added, updated or deleted from the admin screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:430
msgid "(action) Import of questions: all questions were deleted first (replace mode; question ids change), then fired once after the questions were inserted (not once per question). Questions inserted by the import do not fire fqi3_question_created."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:434
msgid "(filter) The question rows returned by the REST endpoints /quizzes, /quizzes/{id} and /quizzes/level/{name}, after the API cache. Do not change the ids, the number of options or the \"answer\" index."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:438
msgid "(filter) Suffix added to the REST API cache keys. Return a stable value (for example a language slug) when an add-on changes the content of a response per request, so one variant is never served from another variant's cache entry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:442
msgid "(action) The core is loaded. Boot add-ons from here (or from plugins_loaded at priority 10+): WordPress loads \"form-quizz-fqi3-xxx/\" plugins before \"form-quizz-fqi3/\", so the core constants and classes do not exist while an add-on main file is being included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:446
msgid "(action) A server-side attempt was created. Fired once per attempt, for logged-in users only. attempt_id is always greater than 0."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:450
msgid "(action) An attempt was completed. Fired exactly once per attempt, for logged-in users only, after the server checked that its questions were served, and with a score computed by the server from the submitted answers (the score sent by the browser is ignored). attempt_id is always greater than 0."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:454
msgid "(action) Before the results are displayed. Only trust it when $verified is true (logged-in user: level and score recorded by the server). It is also fired at page render with placeholder values and $verified = false, and for visitors with browser-supplied values: never use an unverified call to grant points, badges or data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:458
msgid "(filter) Whether the current user may request the questions of a level. Runs on every request: keep callbacks cheap (cached lookups, no remote call). The core rules (levels flagged free for visitors) give the initial value; the filter has the final say, so it can restrict a level or open it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:462
msgid "(filter) Exempts a user from the daily quiz limit of free members for the requested level. Only evaluated once the limit is reached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:466
msgid "(filter) Lock state of a level in the level picker: a padlock, a message and an optional link instead of a selectable option. Display only, the server-side access check is fqi3_user_can_access_level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:470
msgid "(action) Fired when the results container is rendered, before any quiz is played, with placeholder values: never use its arguments as a result. Use fqi3_quiz_attempt_completed for verified data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:474
msgid "(filter) Minimum seconds per question between the questions being served and the completion of the quiz (default 1, 0 disables the check)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:478
msgid "(action) Inject a top panel into the core questions screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:482
msgid "(filter) Append custom actions HTML to each question row (View Questions table)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:486
msgid "(filter) Inject tabs/sections into the core Settings page. Defined in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:489
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

